        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Sandusky Township, Ohio?\n\nAnswer A: 459\n  about: Sandusky Township, Ohio\n  sense: 2020 United States Census (the document does not state it)\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"As of the 2010 census the population was 459.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 1,234\n  about: Sandusky Township, Ohio\n  sense: 2020 United States Census\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: United States Census Bureau\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"As of the 2010 census the population was 1,234.\" [document 3]; \"population 1,234 statement is subject of 2020 United States Census determination method or standard census point in time 1 April 2020\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Sandusky Township, Crawford County, Ohio Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States. As of the 2010 census the population was 459. Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township. Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part. Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties. The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January\nDocument 2: from Wikimedia project Spanish Wikipedia located in the administrative territorial entity Crawford County 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia coordinate location 40°51'5 '' N, 82°49'22 '' W 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project English Wikipedia population 1,234 statement is subject of 2020 United States Census determination method or standard census point in time 1 April 2020 1 reference stated in 2020 United States Census retrieved 1 January 2022 reference URL https : //data.census.gov/cedsci/table? t=Populations % 20and % 20People & g=0100000US, % 241600000 & y=2020 editor United States Census Bureau 1,234 determination method or\nDocument 3: Sandusky Township, Crawford County, Ohio Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States. As of the 2010 census the population was 1,234. Located in the eastern part of the county, it borders the following townships: No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township. Sandusky Township was named from the Sandusky River, which flows through its southern part. Statewide, other Sandusky Townships are located in Richland and Sandusky counties. The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected in November of odd-numbered years to a four-year term beginning on the following January.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\